     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** The maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin is about 2,550 mg/day (FDA labeling), and most institutions cap it at 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day. Also, 1700 mg is not a standard tablet strength (common strengths are 500, 850, and 1000 mg).\n\nThis may be a typo or a different intended regimen. Please confirm one of these:\n\n1. **Metformin 500 mg PO TID with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n2. **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual IR maximum)\n3. **Metformin 1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n4. Another dose you intend, in which case please confirm it is within labeled limits.\n\nSince the patient has normal kidney function, renal dose reduction isn't a factor. If the patient is on other medications or has a specific indication, let me know and I can factor that in. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
